  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1"><xref target="RFC5586" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5586"/> generalizes the Associated Channel mechanism of <xref target="RFC5085" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5085"/>
to be used for Sections, Label Switched Paths (LSPs), and Pseudowires
(PWs) in MPLS networks.  <xref target="RFC5085" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5085"/> defines the Associated Channel
Header (ACH), and <xref target="RFC5586" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5586"/> generalizes this for use as the Generic
Associated Channel (G-ACh).</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2"><xref target="RFC5586" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5586"/> defines a generalized label-based exception mechanism using
the Generic Associated Channel Label (GAL) to work together with the
ACH for use with LSPs but prohibits GAL usage with PWs.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-3">This document removes the restriction imposed by <xref target="RFC5586" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC5586"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="conventions-used-in-this-document" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-conventions-used-in-this-document">Conventions Used in This Document</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">The key words &quot;<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL NOT</bcp14>&quot;,
&quot;<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>&quot;, and &quot;<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>&quot; in this
document are to be interpreted as described in <xref target="RFC2119" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2119"/>.</t>
